# PHASE 13 — Create EKS Cluster

Now comes one of the most important steps.

We'll create:

```text
EKS Cluster
Name: wanderlust
Region: us-west-1
```

First verify AWS:

```bash
aws sts get-caller-identity
```

Then:

```bash
aws configure get region
```

It should return:

```text
us-west-1
```

Now create the cluster control plane.

```bash
eksctl create cluster \
  --name wanderlust \
  --region us-west-1 \
  --version 1.30 \
  --without-nodegroup
```

### What this does

`eksctl` will create AWS infrastructure for:

```text
EKS
VPC
Subnets
Security groups
IAM resources
Control plane
```

This can take several minutes.

**Do not close your SSH session while it is running.**

